#[summary("목록의 최댓값과 합: 재귀 술어로 쓴 계약을 귀납 보조 정리로 한정 기호 계약에 잇는다 (BVB vc-vv0039, ADR-0062, backlog T1-18)")]
mod ml {
    spec fn non_empty(a: &[i64]) -> bool {
        a.len() > 0
    }

    // The first `n` elements hold `r`: a recursive predicate.
    spec fn contains_prefix(a: &[i64], n: usize, r: i64) -> bool
        decreases n,
    {
        if n == 0 { false } else { a[n - 1] == r || contains_prefix(a, n - 1, r) }
    }

    spec fn ge_prefix(a: &[i64], n: usize, m: i64) -> bool {
        forall|j: usize| j < n ==> #[trigger] a[j] <= m
    }

    spec fn max_upto(a: &[i64], k: usize, m: i64) -> bool {
        1 <= k && k <= a.len() && contains_prefix(a, k, m) && ge_prefix(a, k, m)
    }

    spec fn prefix_ok(a: &[i64], n: usize, r: i64) -> bool {
        n <= a.len() && contains_prefix(a, n, r)
    }

    // The same with a quantifier: some index below `n` holds `r`.
    spec fn has_index_below(a: &[i64], n: usize, r: i64) -> bool {
        !(forall|i: usize| i < n ==> #[trigger] a[i] != r)
    }

    // Recursion to quantifier, by induction on `n`. Without it the step
    // from `contains_prefix` to the quantifier needs an induction the
    // solver does not do (backlog T1-14: the judge was undecided).
    #[uses(contains_prefix, has_index_below, prefix_ok)]
    proof fn contains_has_index(a: &[i64], n: usize, r: i64)
        requires prefix_ok(a, n, r),
        ensures has_index_below(a, n, r),
        decreases n,
    {
        if a[n - 1] != r {
            contains_has_index(a, n - 1, r);
        }
    }

    // The hidden contract of the task: the result is an element and at
    // least every element.
    spec fn is_max(a: &[i64], r: i64) -> bool {
        has_index_below(a, a.len(), r) && ge_prefix(a, a.len(), r)
    }

    // The loop keeps the recursive invariant (each step unfolds the
    // definition once); the lemma turns it into the hidden contract.
    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(contains_prefix, ge_prefix, has_index_below, is_max, max_upto, non_empty, prefix_ok)]
    fn max_of_list(lst: &[i64]) -> (r: i64)
        requires non_empty(lst),
        ensures is_max(lst, r),
    {
        let mut m: i64 = lst[0];
        for k in 1..lst.len()
            invariant max_upto(lst, k, m),
        {
            if lst[k] > m {
                m = lst[k];
            }
        }
        proof {
            contains_has_index(lst, lst.len(), m);
        }
        m
    }

    spec fn sum_to(a: &[u64], n: usize) -> u64
        decreases n,
    {
        if n == 0 { 0 } else { sum_to(a, n - 1) + a[n - 1] }
    }

    spec fn within(a: &[u64], i: usize, j: usize) -> bool {
        i <= j && j <= a.len()
    }

    spec fn sum_le(a: &[u64], i: usize, j: usize) -> bool {
        sum_to(a, i) <= sum_to(a, j)
    }

    // A prefix sum is at most a longer one.
    #[uses(sum_le, sum_to, within)]
    proof fn sum_grows(a: &[u64], i: usize, j: usize)
        requires within(a, i, j),
        ensures sum_le(a, i, j),
        decreases j,
    {
        if i < j {
            sum_grows(a, i, j - 1);
        }
    }

    spec fn total_small(a: &[u64]) -> bool {
        sum_to(a, a.len()) <= 1000000
    }

    spec fn is_sum(a: &[u64], s: u64) -> bool {
        s == sum_to(a, a.len())
    }

    // A bound on the whole sum bounds every running sum: the lemma, called
    // in the loop body, shows the addition cannot overflow.
    #[effects(pure)]
    #[uses(is_sum, sum_le, sum_to, total_small, within)]
    fn total(a: &[u64]) -> (r: u64)
        requires total_small(a),
        ensures is_sum(a, r),
    {
        let mut s: u64 = 0;
        for i in 0..a.len()
            invariant s == sum_to(a, i),
        {
            proof {
                sum_grows(a, i + 1, a.len());
            }
            s = s + a[i];
        }
        s
    }

    #[effects(io)]
    #[uses(contains_prefix, ge_prefix, has_index_below, is_max, non_empty, sum_to, total_small)]
    fn main() -> () {
        let xs: [i64; 5] = [3, -7, 12, 12, 0];
        print_i64(max_of_list(&xs));
        let ys: [i64; 3] = [-4, -9, -2];
        print_i64(max_of_list(&ys));
        let zs: [u64; 4] = [10, 200, 3000, 40000];
        print_u64(total(&zs));
    }
}
